  "body": "**Update at 6e381cc81 (review rework):** A selected Arc on an Outside ring pass with no air room is now refused by name (`OUTSIDE_AIR_REFUSAL`). The op posts no ramp stand-in. The pins are now `outside_pocket_arc_without_air_is_refused` and `outside_pocket_selected_entry_keeps_one_warning`. The PR comment 7136819007 has the details and the gate results. Where the text below says that Arc keeps a ramp stand-in on Outside, this update replaces it.\n\n## What changed\n\nA plain 2D Pocket with \"Pass starts at: Outside\" and no stock known has no air room (#3746). Before this change, two entries were notes only:\n\n- With Arc, a later pass start in material took a ramp along the pass (`descent_dive::entry_restart`).\n- With Plunge, the pass link plunged into uncut stock with no note.\n\n`entry_status_lines` dropped the notes, and no warning was posted.\n\nNow, on a start-side ladder (`Motion::cleared_links`, the #3316 link law):\n\n- Each named stand-in entry (a ramp, a helix, an axial dive or a plunge) writes the marker `ENTRY_STAND_IN_NOTE`. The op posts one advisory `Warning::EntryStandIn { at, entries }` that counts the stand-ins.\n- A pass link that plunges into a pass start in material writes `PLUNGE_INTO_STOCK_NOTE`. The op posts one advisory `Warning::PlungeIntoStock`. If the op already posts `EntryNotRecommended` for the selected Plunge, it does not post this second warning. Thus the plunge is named once.\n- `entry_status_lines` shows each stand-in note as a `warning: Entry: ... - fix: ...` line. The two marker notes add no line, because the op warning is already in the status area.\n- MCP names the new kinds `entry_stand_in` and `plunge_into_stock`.\n\nDecision: `docs/decisions/3884-start-side-entry-warnings.md`. Arc with no air room keeps a safe, named stand-in with a Warning. It does not refuse, because a refusal would refuse every plain Outside pocket that uses the default Arc and has no stock.\n\nThe new code is in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/entry_warn.rs`. The changes to `generate.rs` and `types.rs` add only a few lines each. Both files were already over 400 lines.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `camcraft-motion` `pass_start_engagement::outside_pocket_arc_ramp_is_a_warning` (pin 1): the band pocket with no stock and Arc has named stand-ins, and has exactly one `EntryStandIn` warning that counts them.\n- `pass_start_engagement::outside_pocket_plunge_into_stock_is_one_warning` (pin 2): the same pocket with Plunge has more than one plunge, and has exactly one warning that names the plunge.\n- `camcraft-ui` lib `approach_page::top_stock_tests::each_stand_in_entry_is_a_warning_line` (pin 3): the four stand-in note forms from the review are warning lines.\n\nRed first: the pins use the new API (`entry_warnings`, `entry_stand_ins`, the marker notes), so they do not compile on `main`. Without the API, main has no warning and no status line for these notes. The review of #3872 proved this with a probe.\n\n## Gates\n\n- Targeted pins: green.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` (`CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=6`): 324 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (76.7 min); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean.\n- Heavy steps (P1 under the safety floor): `cargo xtask gate heavy --only \"app heavy: offset_pass_start\"` ok (1146 s); `--only \"app heavy: pocket_pass_start\"` ok (10 s).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No app-level test that reads the op warnings for this pocket. The op adds the result of `entry_warnings` with one line in `generate.rs`.\n- The stand-ins of Auto ladders show as warning lines on the op page, but they post no op warning (out of scope; see the decision).\n\nChangelog: A 2D Pocket with \"Pass starts at\" Inside or Outside now posts a warning for each entry that is not the selected one, and for a selected Plunge that plunges into uncut stock. Before, these were notes only.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #3884\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
